From 5c16669abbf26ae38f23a56f46a7a3bd4cb35fc9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ricardo Zuasti <rzuasti@pm.me>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 10:28:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat: send and answer retry requests

Needs libsignal-service's retry request support.

- Received::DecryptionError carries the DecryptionFailure, so clients
  can send its retry request (Manager::send_retry_request); it now also
  fires for unsealed messages.
- Retry requests for this device arrive as Received::RetryRequest
  instead of DecryptionError. One naming our current ratchet key with
  the requesting device archives that session.
- send_message and send_message_to_group return the message as it
  went out (SentContent), with the recipients it reached, for clients
  to keep and resend with Manager::resend_content.
- Manager::send_null_message starts a new session after a retry
  request archived one.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
